<p>From what I understand, the general gist of it is this; the trees started out as memetic anomalies that would rapidly grow when not observed by humans, but when observed by humans would shrink and at the same time infiltrate the human's brain, doing its memetic magic in their mind and killing them. The implication is that the trees purposely grew in certain ways to maximize the amount of humans that saw it, so it could take root in as many minds as possible. Then someone working at the antimemetics department managed to attach some sort of filter/antimeme/antimemetic filter to the trees, making it so humans could still <em>sorta</em> perceive it- enough to the point where the tree's growth is halted but not enough so that the trees could infiltrate the person's mind. The Foundation worker moved the trees to corwded areas so their growth would be constantly held in check, some antimemetic stuff happened to the worker who did it, and now the Foundation doesn't remember the truth behind the trees, and so they just leave them be.</p>

